<section id="title" class="intro">
    <div id="intro" class="intro-copy">
        <span id="about" class="anchor-target"></span>
        <h1 id="page-title" tabindex="-1">Brian Morris</h1>
        <p class="lead">Halton Hills, ON</p>
        <p>I've been learning how to perfect a campsite setup for longer than I can remember. These days, it starts with a well-angled tarp and bungees at each corner. I've found the same satisfaction in:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Adjusting strategies in hockey</li>
            <li>Balancing dynamics in a concert band</li>
            <li>Finding the right exposure for a photo</li>
            <li>Fine-tuning the outhaul on a sailboat</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Long before I recognized it as a skill, I had developed an instinct for learning how systems work, identifying what matters most, and finding the improvements that make the greatest impact.</strong></p>
        <p>When I started exploring technology, that same approach came naturally. What started as a curiosity became a way to turn ideas into practical solutions, automate tedious processes, and solve increasingly complex problems.</p>
        <p><strong>Today, I lead a team supporting a major bank's enterprise big data platform, where I apply that same approach to keeping critical systems running reliably and finding ways to make them better.</strong></p>
        <div class="link-row"><a class="button" href="mailto:contact@brianmorris.info">Say hello &#8599;</a></div>
    </div>
    <picture class="portrait"><img src="/img/Brian-Morris-Central-Park-Square.jpg" alt="Brian Morris in Central Park" width="400" height="400" fetchpriority="high"></picture>
</section>
<section id="experience" class="page-section">
    <div class="section-label"><h2>Current role</h2></div>
    <div class="section-copy">
        <h3>Team Lead – Enterprise DaaS &amp; Big Data L2</h3>
        <p class="caption">Tata Consultancy Services · Supporting TD Bank · Since 2020</p>
        <p>I lead an L2 production support team for TD Bank's enterprise <a href="https://www.databricks.com/blog/how-databricks-lakehouse-helping-power-new-era-td-bank-groups-data-transformation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Data as a Service (DaaS) platform</a>. Our team oversees the daily operation of data ingestion, transformation, and extraction pipelines, investigating application failures, coordinating recovery from infrastructure outages, and ensuring critical data processing continues reliably.</p>
        <p>My role combines hands-on technical investigation with team leadership and incident management. I analyze application logs, SQL, job metadata, and scheduling dependencies to identify root causes, assess downstream impacts, and determine recovery strategies. I also coordinate across development, infrastructure, and business teams to resolve incidents, manage escalations, and identify opportunities to improve operational efficiency and platform reliability.</p>
        <p>I've supported the <a href="https://betakit.com/td-cloud-data-migration/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">migration of hundreds of data sources and ETL workloads from on-premises Hadoop to Microsoft Azure</a>, helping maintain operations throughout the transition. Working across both environments has given me a broad understanding of enterprise data platforms, from the underlying infrastructure to the complex dependencies that connect individual processes. It's also reinforced my interest in finding practical ways to simplify operations, reduce recurring issues, and make systems more reliable.</p>
    </div>
</section>
<section id="projects" class="page-section">
    <div class="section-label"><h2>Projects</h2></div>
    <div class="section-copy project-list">
        <article class="project-feature">
        <h3>Acton Citizens' Band website</h3>
        <p>I designed and maintain the band's public website, bringing concert information, recruitment, junior band programs, and contact details into one place. The work includes organizing content for visitors and keeping it current as the band's activities change.</p>
        <p>Built with React and TypeScript, the site uses Firebase Hosting and Cloudflare, with Three.js powering interactive 3D instruments.</p>
        <a class="button button--secondary" href="https://actoncitizensband.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit the band website <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span><span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
    </article>
        <article class="project-feature">
            <h3>Meridian's learning management system</h3>
            <p>After completing my co-op terms at Meridian Credit Union, I was contracted by the Learning and Development team to build a new learning management system. It enabled the team to organize custom and external learning content and control how it was presented through a clean, intuitive interface.</p>
            <p>Built on SharePoint using JavaScript, CSS, and the SharePoint Client-Side Object Model, the LMS combined SharePoint’s content management capabilities and Meridian’s existing intranet with a purpose-built learning experience.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="project-feature">
            <h3>Soo Food Finder</h3>
            <p>While studying at Algoma University, I was recommended by my professors to help develop Soo Food Finder, a community tool connecting people in Sault Ste. Marie with local food resources. I built a content management interface using PHP and Firebase, enabling administrators to maintain and update the food-access information.</p>
            <p class="caption">The project is no longer online.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
<section id="outside-work" class="page-section">
    <div class="section-label"><h2>Away from the keyboard</h2></div>
    <div id="community" class="section-copy">
        <p>I spend my summers camping at <a href="https://www.ontarioparks.ca/park/killbear" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Killbear Provincial Park</a>, exploring Georgian Bay by boat, sailboat, or kayak. The rocky shoreline, windswept pines, starry nights, and familiar faces make it my favourite place in the world. There's a sense of community among the regulars: people who share a love of the park, always have a story to share, and make returning feel like coming home.</p>
        <p>I also enjoy travelling, especially planning the trip: researching destinations, working out routes, and piecing together an itinerary that leaves room to explore. Trying new foods is one of my favourite parts of visiting somewhere new, and there's always room in the itinerary for something good to eat. I always have my camera in hand, and I take so many photos that I've had to develop my own tools and scripts to organize them all.</p>
        <p>I've played percussion with the Acton Citizens' Band since 2005, in concert and on parade, and have mentored younger musicians through the Acton Junior Band. Founded in 1872, the band is now <%= new Date().getFullYear() - 1872 %> years old and entirely volunteer-run. Through concerts, parades, and opportunities for young musicians, it brings people together and keeps community music a part of life in Acton.</p>
        <p>I play forward in hockey, and I cheer the loudest for Team Canada.</p>
    </div>
</section>
